// What asks for a memory in Windreach (bible 10, docs/design/offerings.md; `Offerings`). The offer command gives it;
// can_offer(asker, memory) and offered(asker) ask. A given memory is gone for good. Brek is the fledgling Idrenne
// calls to at the leap (Gate_Idrenne_Leap). The young stand on a place, not a dare (Gate_Lip).

title: Gate_Brek
---
<<if not has_flag("windreach.leap.done")>>
    Brek: Don't look at me. I'm not on the stones. I'm near them. #still #line:0b7beb4
    <<stop>>
<<endif>>
<<if offered("gate_brek")>>
    Brek: I'm on her fire's stone. Next spring, I jump. She says spring comes when it comes. #still #line:0adb0d9
    <<stop>>
<<endif>>
Brek: You jumped. The air knew you. It doesn't know me. I asked it. #still #line:028a2c5
Brek: Idrenne says you stand on a place, not a dare. I haven't got a place. #still #line:08b8cc1
-> Idrenne's. Her fire, the year they said no. <<if can_offer("gate_brek", "idrenne.standing_place")>> #line:005136c
    <<voice surveyor windreach>>
    <<offer gate_brek idrenne.standing_place>>
    Brek: Her fire. Where she was standing. I can stand on that. #line:045e0d1
    Brek: Not today. But look. I'm on the stone. Sing, somebody. Ha. I sound like her. #line:05ae6ca
-> Find your own. #line:063d5a7
    <<voice warden windreach>>
    Brek: That's what she says. Then she laughs. I don't know why that helps. #still #line:02ea62e
-> ... #line:0709381
    <<voice drift windreach>>
    Brek: You stood like that on the lip. Quiet. Then you went. #still #line:0b6a637
===
